earch of a lost function. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>46</volume>:<fpage>2</fpage>&#x02013;4.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15820687</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="journal">Tamura, N., Y. Ogawa, H. Chusho, K. Nakamura, K. Nakao, M. Suda, M. Kasahara, R. Hashimoto, G. Katsuura, M. Mukoyama, et al. <year>2000</year>. Cardiac fibrosis in mice lacking brain natriuretic peptide. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>97</volume>:<fpage>4239</fpage>&#x02013;4244.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10737768</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib35"><citation citation-type="journal">Walent, J.H., B.W. Porter, and T.F. Martin. <year>1992</year>. A novel 145 kd brain cytosolic protein reconstitutes Ca(2&#x0002b;)-regulated secretion in permeable neuroendocrine cells. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>70</volume>:<fpage>765</fpage>&#x02013;775.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1516133</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib36"><citation citation-type="journal">Wennerberg, K., K.L. Rossman, and C.J. Der. <year>2005</year>. The Ras superfamily at a glance. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>118</volume>:<fpage>843</fpage>&#x02013;846.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15731001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib37"><citation citation-type="journal">Yu, Y., S. Li, X. Xu, Y. Li, K. Guan, E. Arnold, and J. Ding. <year>2005</year>. Structural basis for the unique biological function of small GTPase RHEB. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>280</volume>:<fpage>17093</fpage>&#x02013;17100.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15728574</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib38"><citation citation-type="journal">Zucman-Rossi, J., P. Legoix, and G. Thomas. <year>1996</year>. Identification of new members of the Gas2 and Ras families in the 22q12 chromosome region. <source>Genomics.</source> <volume>38</volume>:<fpage>247</fpage>&#x02013;254.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8975699</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>